{"text": "Veldhoek Fietsen & Outdoor B.V.\nPrivacy Office / Functionaris Gegevensbescherming\nCroeselaan 318, 3521 CG Utrecht, Nederland\nKvK 70418829 - BTW NL861204733B01\n\nBY REGISTERED POST AND E-MAIL                                   Utrecht, 7 April 2026\nOur ref: DSAR-2026-0193            Your ref: your e-mail of 11 March\n\nFrau Annelies Terpstra\nLindenthalgürtel 48\n50935 Köln\nDeutschland\na.terpstra84@postfach.example\n\nSubject: Your request for access under Article 15 GDPR\n\nDear Ms Terpstra,\n\nYou asked us on 11 March for a copy of the personal data we hold about you. We\nconfirmed your identity by telephone on 18.03.2026 (call taken by Fenna Zuidema of\ncustomer service, who rang you back on +49 221 5550 187). This letter is our\nresponse under Regulation (EU) 2016/679. It is sent within the one-month period of\nArt. 12(3); we did not need the extension.\n\n1. Who we are. Veldhoek is the controller. Our Data Protection Officer is\nJoris Hendrickx (fg@veldhoek-fietsen.example, 030 555 0142). Outside counsel,\nKruisberg Advocaten N.V., reviewed the annexes; mr. Hendrickx signs for us.\n\n2. What we hold (full export in Annex A, 24 pages).\n\n   Identity and contact   customer no. K-4471902; name; date of birth 23-09-1984;\n                          the Köln address above and your previous address,\n                          Oudegracht 211 bis, 3511 NH Utrecht (until August 2023);\n                          mobile 0049 171 5550 163; German tax ID you gave us for the\n                          lease-bike invoice, 48 205 916 374.\n   Online account         username annelies_t84, created 2 June 2019. We store only a\n                          salted hash of your password, not the password itself.\n   Orders                 14 orders between 2019 and 26 February 2026, most recently order\n                          VF-2026-118834 (Trekking E-bike, € 3.249,00) and the return of\n                          RMA-55120, refunded EUR 189,95 on 03.03.2026.\n   Payment                SEPA mandate VFM-000482771 on IBAN DE71 0539 3195 1175 4199 10\n                          (BIC GENODED1SPR, Sparda-Genossenschaftsbank Rheinland eG); a Mastercard stored as\n                          5553 18** **** 0072, expiry 11/27. We never hold the security code.\n   Customer-service notes 6 entries. One, dated 9 January 2026, records that you returned the\n                          saddle because of a knee replacement last autumn. See point 5.\n   Marketing              newsletter consent given 2 June 2019, withdrawn 14-01-2026; loyalty\n                          card 6340 0091 7725 4418 with 1.240 points.\n\n3. Technical data (Annex B). Our web shop and app logged:\n   - sign-ins from 203.0.113.47 (Köln, 31 times), 198.51.100.212 (Utrecht, until 2023)\n     and once from 2001:db8:4c1a:9e::2f on 22 December 2025;\n   - app installation ID 7f3c1a9e-52b0-4d1e-9a6f-0c2e81d4b7a3 on a Google Pixel 8a\n     (Android 15), advertising ID c41d77e0-9b2a-4f6e-8d35-1a60b2f9e4c8, and an older\n     phone with IMEI 35 738055 554584 2 that we recorded for the theft-insurance add-on;\n   - the frame number of your bike, WVF24T0381176, and the serial of its\n     battery, BT-E8036-22K4417;\n   - Wi-Fi MAC 9c:2e:a1:4f:07:d3 seen by the in-store network in our Utrecht shop.\n\n4. Recipients. Delivery data went to Postillon Pakketdienst B.V. (tracking\n3SPOST881204417). Warranty work was passed to our German service partner\nBrückner Zweiradtechnik, Aachener Straße 1120, Köln (Matthias Brückner,\nm.brueckner@brueckner-zweirad.example). Herr Brückner holds only your name, phone and frame number.\n\n5. The health remark. The service note about your knee should not have been\nwritten down. It was not needed for the return (Art. 6(1)(b)) and we had no\nbasis to keep health data. We erased the sentence on 1 April 2026; the\nunredacted note is shown to you once, in Annex C, so you can see what was held.\nNo other record mentions your health, and the profile label \"lives alone, 40-45, no car\"\nhas been deleted from our marketing system as well.\n\n6. Your rights. You may ask for rectification (Article 16) or erasure (Article 17),\nand you may complain to the Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens or to the authority in\nNordrhein-Westfalen.\n\nA secure copy of the annexes is at\nhttps://privacy.veldhoek-fietsen.example/dsar/DSAR-2026-0193 ; the one-time\naccess code VH-7Q2M-K9XD was sent by SMS to the number ending 0163.\n\nKind regards,\n\nJ. Hendrickx\nData Protection Officer", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "614 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Annelies Terpstra", "Fenna Zuidema", "Joris Hendrickx", "J. Hendrickx"], "companies": ["Veldhoek Fietsen & Outdoor B.V.", "Kruisberg Advocaten N.V.", "Sparda-Genossenschaftsbank Rheinland eG", "veldhoek-fietsen", "Postillon Pakketdienst B.V.", "Brückner Zweiradtechnik"]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.19999999925494194, "modelMs": 34684.699999999255, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "names"], "detections": [{"start": 0, "end": 31, "text": "Veldhoek Fietsen & Outdoor B.V.", "kind": "company", "source": "model", "canonical": "Veldhoek Fietsen & Outdoor B.V."}, {"start": 129, "end": 137, "text": "70418829", "kind": "account", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "70418829"}, {"start": 144, "end": 158, "text": "NL861204733B01", "kind": "record", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "NL861204733B01"}, {"start": 233, "end": 245, "text": "7 April 2026", "kind": "date", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "7 April 2026"}, {"start": 255, "end": 269, "text": "DSAR-2026-0193", "kind": "record", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "DSAR-2026-0193"}, {"start": 306, "end": 314, "text": "11 March", "kind": "date", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "11 March"}, {"start